{"duration_api_ms":25824,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d2cbef7b-22f2-4471-b9b1-760b13dc4877","total_cost_usd":0.9699162000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":104408,"cache_read_input_tokens":400681,"output_tokens":2725,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":710},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":104408,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":727,"cache_read_input_tokens":201099,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72733},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2725,"cacheReadInputTokens":400681,"cacheCreationInputTokens":104408,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9699162000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":710,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `labels/coder-1.json` and coded the `egi-draft-a1v2` row as **rung 2, \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents.\"** It rests on one vote, so code will tier it `single-source`.\n\n**Evidence.** On 2024-06-13, during her current term, she voted Aye on Senate final passage of AB 1955 (2023-2024). That was the vote on the text the Senate inserted, which became the chaptered law. The tally was 29-8. Eight of 40 members voted No, so it is not near-unanimous.\n\n**Why rung 2.** The law's operative Section 220.5 forbids schools, districts and their boards to enact or enforce \"any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require an employee or a contractor to disclose\" a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That matches rung 2.\n\n**Why not rung 1.** The law removes any duty to tell parents, but it never says staff must withhold the information. So it does not reach \"require staff to keep a student's gender identity from parents.\"\n\n**Calls a reviewer may want to check:**\n- **Preemption.** I coded the vote `on-question` rather than `adjacent`, even though the law forbids local rules. Rung 2 is itself about forbidding those rules, which is the exception the codebook allows.\n- **Single subject.** I treated the bill as single-subject. It has three parts — resources for families of LGBTQ pupils, a ban on retaliating against school staff, and the disclosure ban — but all of them concern LGBTQ pupils' rights at school.\n- **Qualifier.** The section keeps the phrase \"unless otherwise required by state or federal law.\" I did not treat it as stopping a match with rung 2.\n\nI logged no quotes and no `needs_source` entries, because neither snapshot contains her own words.\n\nSeparately, several connectors (Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey, WorkOS) need to be authorized in claude.ai connector settings, and the GitHub plugin failed to connect. None of them was needed for this task.","ttft_ms":8266,"type":"result","duration_ms":28013,"uuid":"ac32dc1b-a13d-4336-b054-0cbf7dd60a97","ttft_stream_ms":1659,"time_to_request_ms":139,"first_content_frame_ms":1660,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
